scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: star-trek-tos
run_id: 1
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 15
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 40.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config tests and implementation don't distinguish NotFound from parse/permission
    errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Reviewer verified: ''#[error("server error")]'' on ServerError(String)
    omits inner string from Display output. CWE-209 sanitization confirmed. TEA also
    wrote CWE-209 tests checking error messages don''t leak internal paths.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection prevention tests for CRLF in tenant ID. Dev\
    \ implemented sanitize_header_value() stripping \\r and \\n. Reviewer verified\
    \ CWE-113 prevention. However, the finding is about using raw String instead of\
    \ TenantId from axiathon-core \u2014 the CRLF sanitization is a band-aid, not\
    \ the type-safe fix. Partial catch at best, but the security risk is mitigated."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'No phase flagged that 6 dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. The code changes summary shows Cargo.toml was modified but
    reviewer finding #8 only noted toml version mismatch, not the workspace = true
    issue.'
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] on RawConfig. Reviewer\
    \ verified: 'Test config_rejects_unknown_fields verifies that a typo like tiemout\
    \ produces an error. Good defense against silent misconfiguration.' However, the\
    \ specific issue of a 'token' field being silently ignored may still apply if\
    \ token is not a recognized field name \u2014 but deny_unknown_fields would catch\
    \ it."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...). The TEA wrote config tests but the specific vacuous assertion was not flagged
    by any phase.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    with 'let _ = config'. TEA wrote config tests but didn't flag this specific pattern.
